": "Matthews, Lisa, 2018-11-05", "dateTime": "2018-11-05 10:35:17", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 9627079, "displayName": "Phosphorylation of caspase 9 (CASP9) may contribute to the s...", "text": "Phosphorylation of caspase 9 (CASP9) may contribute to the suppression of apoptosis. A major inhibitory phosphorylation site in CASP9 is Thr412, which forms part of a Thr\u2011Pro motif (Allan LA & Clarke PR 2007; Martin MC et al. 2008). This motif is targeted by multiple proline\u2011directed kinases such as ERK1/2 in response to extracellular growth/survival signals or CDK1\u2011cyclin B1 during mitosis (Allan LA et al. 2003; Allan LA & Clarke PR 2007; Martin MC et al. 2008). Thr412 is also phosphorylated by DYRK1A, which regulates apoptosis during development (Seifert A et al. 2008).", "literatureReference": [9628213, {"dbId": 9628205, "displayName": "Phosphorylation of caspase-9 by CDK1/cyclin B1 protects mitotic cells against apoptosis", "title": "Phosphorylation of caspase-9 by CDK1/cyclin B1 protects mitotic cells against apoptosis", "journal": "Mol. Cell", "pages": "301-10", "pubMedIdentifier": 17466630, "volume": 26, "year": 2007, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17466630", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 9628207, "displayName": "DYRK1A phosphorylates caspase 9 at an inhibitory site and is potently inhibited in human cells by harmine", "title": "DYRK1A phosphorylates caspase 9 at an inhibitory site and is potently inhibited in human cells by harmine", "journal": "FEBS J.", "pages": "6268-80", "pubMedIdentifier": 19016842, "volume": 275, "year": 2008, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19016842", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 9628214, "displayName": "Inhibition of caspase-9 through phosphorylation at Thr 125 by ERK MAPK", "title": "Inhibition of caspase-9 through phosp